# .publication-denylist — D8 choice (a): publication-safe pattern notation.
# Per-repo D8 ruling recorded: https://github.com/caty-ai/alpha-nightshift/issues/46
# Format: NAME<TAB>REGEX (Python re, IGNORECASE). One rule per line.
#
# D8-(a) notation, following the checker's own embedded fixture
# (tools/check_publication_gate.py, SELFTEST_DENYLIST, `acme[-_ ]secret`): where a
# rule would otherwise contain a protected literal, a character class splits it, so
# this committed file does not publish the strings it protects while the regex still
# matches them. The checker path-excludes this file from its own scan, so it is
# structurally unable to catch a violation here — tests/test_publication_denylist.sh
# is what actually enforces it (issue #50).
#
# The invariant is "no rule may match this file", not "every rule is split":
# HOME_ABS_PATH and TAILSCALE_CGNAT_IP are generic shape patterns that carry no
# protected literal, so there is nothing in them to split. Rules that name a
# specific protected string are all split, with no exceptions — an exception list
# would be the thing that rots.
#
# NOTE ON SCOPE OF THIS FILE'S PROTECTION: splitting a literal defeats a substring
# search of the published blob. It does not make the value secret from a human
# reader, and it does nothing about older commits that spelled the value out. Any
# rule here whose value must genuinely not reach the public must be handled by
# history treatment before the flip, not by notation (seat finding, PR #51; #55).
#
# Scope: repo-specific protected literals only — generic secret shapes (tokens,
# private-key blocks) are gitleaks' job (PR-range caller + the pre-flip full-history
# sweep), and duplicating them here would flag the guard tests' deliberate fixtures.
HOME_ABS_PATH	/Users/[a-z0-9_-]+/
# Personal-account references. The rule is adjacency to punctuation: the account ID
# touching any locator or delimiter character on either side is a reference that
# carries context (repo, host, mailbox, profile, serialized field, link target). The
# ID isolated by whitespace is NOT matched, because .github/risk-reviewers.txt must
# name it on a line of its own by contract — that roster line is the entire reason
# this rule is not the blunt "any mention" rule (issue #50).
#
# Six review seats each demonstrated shapes a narrower version let through; the
# classes below are the union of everything they found: @handle, owner/repo, https
# and scp remotes (with and without a path), email (including plus-tagged), pages
# and blog hosts, social profile paths, query values, KEY=value assignments,
# serialized/quoted fields, and markdown link text.
#
# The checker's own --account-slug backstop only sees github.com / gist /
# <slug>.github.io, so every other shape is uncovered without this rule.
#
# Deliberately over-matches prose that puts punctuation against the ID ("thanks to
# <slug>." or "<slug>, and others"). That direction is fail-closed: the gate names
# the rule in its failure, and prose can be rephrased. Under-matching cannot be
# undone after a flip.
PERSONAL_ACCOUNT_REF	(?:(?<=[@/:="'\[({,])shojikumar[u](?![A-Za-z0-9-])|(?<![A-Za-z0-9-])shojikumar[u][/.@+"'\])},])
FAMILY_VAULT_PATH	SharedHub/famil[y][-_]vault
ALPHA_WIKI_PATH	claude-workspace/alph[a][-_]wiki
TAILSCALE_CGNAT_IP	\b100\.(6[4-9]|[7-9][0-9]|1[01][0-9]|12[0-7])\.[0-9]{1,3}\.[0-9]{1,3}\b
HANDOFF_DIR	_handoff[s]/
